===== README.md [Once] =====
# order-workers

Camunda 8 job workers generated by `bpmnkit worker gen --lang java --build gradle --spring`. No Gradle install needed: `gradlew` is the Gradle Wrapper (Java 21 required).

```sh
./gradlew bootRun        # start the workers (REST, CAMUNDA_REST_ADDRESS, default http://localhost:8080)
./gradlew build   # build and test (Camunda Process Test needs a Docker-compatible runtime)
```

## Job types

- `charge-card` → `handlers/ChargeCardHandler.java`
- `ship.order` → `handlers/ShipOrderHandler.java`

## Ownership

- `src/main/java/**/gen/` is overwritten by `bpmnkit worker gen` (`DO NOT EDIT`). Check drift in CI with `--check`.
- Everything else (handlers, tests, `App.java`, `build.gradle.kts`, `settings.gradle.kts`, the wrapper) is written once and never overwritten.
- Delivery is at-least-once: handlers must be idempotent.
===== build.gradle.kts [Once] =====
// Written once by bpmnkit; yours from now on. Versions are pinned exactly.
plugins {
    java
    id("org.springframework.boot") version "3.5.16"
}

group = "com.example.orderworkers"
version = "0.1.0"

repositories {
    mavenCentral()
}

dependencies {
    implementation("io.camunda:camunda-spring-boot-starter:8.8.47")
    testImplementation("org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-test:3.5.16")
    testImplementation("io.camunda:camunda-process-test-spring:8.8.47")
    testImplementation(platform("org.junit:junit-bom:5.12.2"))
    testImplementation("org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter")
    testRuntimeOnly("org.junit.platform:junit-platform-launcher")
}

springBoot {
    mainClass.set("com.example.orderworkers.App")
}

tasks.withType<JavaCompile>().configureEach {
    options.encoding = "UTF-8"
    options.release.set(21)
}

tasks.test {
    useJUnitPlatform()
}

// Same bytes for the same sources.
tasks.withType<AbstractArchiveTask>().configureEach {
    isPreserveFileTimestamps = false
    isReproducibleFileOrder = true
}
